%T Research on Safety Development of LLM for Tobacco Industry Applications
%@ 9798400718724
%U https://doi.org/10.1145/3800227.3800412
%R 10.1145/3800227.3800412
%X This article analyzes the application of large-scale models in the vertical subdivision field of safety development in the tobacco industry, and seeks to find the most suitable open-source lightweight large-scale models for construction and research. The existing security development models have problems such as high cost, low application efficiency, difficult deployment, and poor scalability combination ability. This article adopts a technical route of evaluation selection, fine-tuning training, and prototype system application to achieve secure development of tobacco industry applications, reduce financial impact, lower trial and error costs, and support the industry's scientific and technological innovation development plan.
