%0 Conference Paper
%T A Declarative Conversion Framework for Legacy CAE Input Systems: Pattern-Based Parsing and Unified Intermediate Representation
%@ 9798400721106
%U https://doi.org/10.1145/3779475.3779498
%R 10.1145/3779475.3779498
%X Traditional computer-aided engineering (CAE) software often relies on rigid, position-sensitive command-line inputs that hinder software migration, localization, and automation. This paper presents a declarative conversion framework that leverages JSON Schema to transform legacy command scripts into a Unified Intermediate Schema (UIS) and automatically generate multi-target code through a template-based pipeline. The framework introduces a pattern-driven parsing engine to overcome the limitations of position-dependent syntaxes, develops a JSON-based UIS to unify and extend diverse command types, and designs a modular generation process that outputs consistent C++ classes and configuration files. Experiments on over one hundred representative commands demonstrate improved accuracy, maintainability, and scalability, highlighting the framework's potential for cross-platform adaptation and modernization of CAE input systems.
%B Proceedings of the 2025 2nd International Conference on Cloud Computing and Big Data
