%T Bridging the Cyberinfrastructure Training Gap: Assessing the Impact of the COMPLECS HPC Training Program for Research End-Users
%@ 9798400723773
%U https://doi.org/10.1145/3785462.3815866
%R 10.1145/3785462.3815866
%X The COMPLECS CyberTraining program addresses the gap between traditional developer-centric high-performance computing training and the practical needs of modern researchers. Using a three-tier curriculum, the program has impacted more than 1,700 participants in its first 30 months, hosting 43 webinars and 5 immersive, multi-day workshops. Here, we review the program’s growth and offer insights for cyberinfrastructure training and improved strategies for user engagement and resource dissemination.
